ield/validate]} {:db/id "q-86429" :question/id #uuid "e6f0245e-794a-58d1-963e-1b63286cc3b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-86429" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=6{x}^{2}+2y$ at the point $(0,1)$ in the direction of the vector $v=3i+5j.$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $v$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)=∇f(a,b)\\cdot u\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $v.$\n\nFirst, we find the unit vector $u$ in the direction of $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{5}^{2}}=\\sqrt{34} \\\\ u & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{34}}(3i+5j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6{x}^{2}+2y)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(6{x}^{2}+2y)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =12x\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇\\,f(0,1) & =(12\\cdot 0)\\,i+2\\,j \\\\  & =2j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{u}^{′}(0,1) & =∇\\,f(0,1)\\cdot u \\\\  & =2j\\cdot (\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{34}}i+\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{34}}j) \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 5}{\\sqrt{34}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\sqrt{34}}{34}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-86429/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd2b430e-fd5d-57ba-bc28-f7c113eda07a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86429"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-36290/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "86ed191c-8281-514c-a6a7-5bcbdb09338e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36290/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "d4b2bc67-f6fa-526b-965f-d373f0f9d9d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value