n\nwhere $u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $v.$\n\nFirst, we find the direction vector and the corresponding unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨0,1⟩-⟨1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,1⟩ \\\\ u & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}}{‖\\overset{\\to }{AB}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}}⟨-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $A(1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{e}^{y}+{x}^{2}y),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{e}^{y}+{x}^{2}y)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{y}+2xy,\\,x{e}^{y}+{x}^{2}⟩ \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,0) & =⟨{e}^{0}+2\\cdot 1\\cdot 0,\\,1\\cdot {e}^{0}+{1}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{u}^{′}(1,0) & =∇f(1,0)\\cdot u \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-36290/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd2b430e-fd5d-57ba-bc28-f7c113eda07a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36290"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130260/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "3df1bb49-be12-579a-be49-02acee544c71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130260/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer/id #uuid "4d2019ec-e80f-557c-be6d-c6b58ef95b53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130260/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "1387ecfa-c811-5dbd-89f9-1d56855c9c6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130260/selection/0734b5ff5a2e78c8beb029dd8cc975013694a0a7f8ae4619b214817f651a55b4" :answer/id #uuid "687ee922-7345-5c51-9050-5eb5519ffb96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130260/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "9c018086-5c23-5a8f-8b15-232c9a5c3892" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130260/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2e33e530-7e03-562a-abfe-728c1d513687" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130260/selection/0734b5ff5a2e78c8beb029dd8cc975013694a0a7f8ae4619b214817f651a55b4" :answer-field/choices ["q-130260/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-130260/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" "q-130260/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-130260/selection/0734b5ff5a2e78c8beb029dd8cc975013694a0a7f8ae4619b214817f651a55b4" "q-130260/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130260" :question/id #uuid "b1939235-4888-56a0-832d-3d89089852b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-130260" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})$ at the point $(0,-1)$ in the direction of the vector $v=3\\,i+4\\,j.$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $v$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)=∇f(a,b)\\cdot u\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $v.$\n\nFirst, we find the unit vector $u$ in the direction of $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}=5 \\\\ u & =\\frac{1}{5}(3\\,i+4\\,j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(0,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}))\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}))\\text{ }j \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}j \\\\ ∇\\,f(0,-1) & =\\frac{2(0)}{{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{2(-1)}{{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\,j \\\\  & =-2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{u}^{′}(0,-1) & =∇\\,f(0,-1)\\cdot u \\\\  & =-2\\,j\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}(3\\,i+4\\,j) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2(4)}{5} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130260/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd2b430e-fd5d-57ba-bc28-f7c113eda07a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130260"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130257/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" :answer/id #uuid "5e58f2ec-e905-5c15-8ed1-3bdd36b6c30c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130257/selection/ce8782833fa4948cd084022417399eb423071769333088dca13d11299860028b" :answer/id #uuid "8a613c31-f47a-5e9c-9110-8be6de36c91f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+2}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130257/selection/7c6b5bc38368b6f9e40db2ccc8d97c72bad3c796a8da6f294b6fc2d08a174be1" :answer/id #uuid "4d6c0613-d577-5ca5-be23-3df167fde053" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130257/selection/6b3d017e6099e9717e9d6cee8710ec7291889ec5f66eeba6121799de3f9d7231" :answer/id #uuid "5cdb3595-7a0a-53db-81b3-618eb321a9fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+4}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130257/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" :answer/id #uuid "1e88a357-c5cc-5568-85ae-94bdda9b4ad6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130257/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c3b339c-645a-5aca-94cb-877c4133c408" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130257/selection/ce8782833fa4948cd084022417399eb423071769333088dca13d11299860028b" :answer-field/choices ["q-130257/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" "q-130257/selection/ce8782833fa4948cd084022417399eb423071769333088dca13d11299860028b" "q-130257/selection/7c6b5bc38368b6f9e40db2ccc8d97c72bad3c796a8da6f294b6fc2d08a174be1" "q-130257/selection/6b3d017e6099e9717e9d6cee8710ec7291889ec5f66eeba6121799de3f9d7231" "q-130257/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130257" :question/id #uuid "4fdbef4a-96b4-5d61-a423-a5d3b28ba07f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130257" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=xy$ at the point $(2,1)$ in the direction of the vector $v=\\sqrt{3}\\,i+j.$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $v$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)=∇f(a,b)\\cdot u\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $v.$\n\nFirst, we find the unit vector $u$ in the direction of $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{1}^{2}}=2 \\\\ u & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}\\,i+j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =y\\,i+x\\,j \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,1) & =i+2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{u}^{′}(2,1) & =∇\\,f(2,1)\\cdot u \\\\  & =(i+2\\,j)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{3}\\,i+j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1(\\sqrt{3})+2(1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+2}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130257/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd2b430e-fd5d-57ba-bc28-f7c113eda07a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130257"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130263/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "543ca7e2-dae8-5a16-9398-3524d45062ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130263/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "e11e3381-95c5-5142-9929-7f7bc8f65b6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130263/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "e01a7e7c-215a-5c91-9229-70341f5ab71a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130263/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "e5af4623-be33-50ee-9b8b-affeaaa1f686" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130263/selection/6b95511de4de11a307ef0b59561676b4ba5acdacebc5c441c2ab3b04050b282b" :answer/id #uuid "26f64e91-56bc-5937-81a1-991402d48081" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130263/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d27610ab-136e-50ea-b6f9-559952982e1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130263/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-130263/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-130263/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-130263/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-130263/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-130263/selection/6b95511de4de11a307ef0b59561676b4ba5acdacebc5c441c2ab3b04050b282b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130263" :question/id #uuid "c6ac9420-587f-5958-bf51-cf604553d217" :question/math-academy-id "q-130263" :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-xy$ at the point $(1,1)$ in the direction of the vector $v=i-j.$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative ${f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $v$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)=∇f(a,b)\\cdot u\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $v.$\n\nFirst, we find the unit vector $u$ in the direction of $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ u & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(i-j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-xy)i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-xy)j \\\\  & =(2x-y)\\,i+(2y-x)\\,j \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,1) & =(2(1)-1)\\,i+(2(1)-1)\\,j \\\\  & =i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{u}^{′}(1,1) & =∇\\,f(1,1)\\cdot u \\\\  & =(i+j)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(i-j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1(1)+1(-1)}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130263/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd2b430e-fd5d-57ba-bc28-f7c113eda07a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130263"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-37080/selection/2fb37e8cc2bfeeab04876d670ca8048cbe842f88f48a546ef24ed826c48a4ed4" :answer/id #uuid "c96d5d44-8cf0-5fb9-9852-354e11fb166d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,\\,-1,\\,6⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37080/selection/504cb6a68b78928eb33e4815b7e46a7f90639c1ac9f7434b48eaf656b3142410" :answer/id #uuid "e709157c-c442-55e7-8de1-60b30f34941e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\pi +3,\\,\\pi ,\\,3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37080/selection/e9c784e27fba202829f7ef524ac5d1d75c8552fd41dbebea427d9c0227b8c048" :answer/id #uuid "60397245-d895-528a-a207-7574581256a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,\\,-\\pi ,\\,3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37080/selection/3822590f241316b51f178bdfaa490791e2c3ecbf7122d8fc448cd66467de4084" :answer/id #uuid "bbeda845-ac3d-5c75-8aab-307df77aabaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,\\,0,\\,6⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37080/selection/1ed6e0a318cd5f48d51f2167baeb63db2b6775eac3cd8d5e83f8a5c492864e7e" :answer/id #uuid "e4555297-09f5-5912-a47c-1297a4cf0890" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\pi +3,\\,-1,\\,6⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37080/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d1aea48-80f6-5016-90d2-19ee585adba4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-37080/selection/1ed6e0a318cd5f48d51f2167baeb63db2b6775eac3cd8d5e83f8a5c492864e7e" :answer-field/choices ["q-37080/selection/2fb37e8cc2bfeeab04876d670ca8048cbe842f88f48a546ef24ed826c48a4ed4" "q-37080/selection/504cb6a68b78928eb33e4815b7e46a7f90639c1ac9f7434b48eaf656b3142410" "q-37080/selection/e9c784e27fba202829f7ef524ac5d1d75c8552fd41dbebea427d9c0227b8c048" "q-37080/selection/3822590f241316b51f178bdfaa490791e2c3ecbf7122d8fc448cd66467de4084" "q-37080/selection/1ed6e0a318cd5f48d51f2167baeb63db2b6775eac3cd8d5e83f8a5c492864e7e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-37080" :question/id #uuid "043c94bf-7651-58ea-abe2-4c89798a1721" :question/math-academy-id "q-37080" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x+y)+3{z}^{2}x$, in what direction does the function increase most rapidly at the point $(1,0,1)?$" :question/worked-solution "At a given point, a function $f(x,y,z)$ increases most rapidly in the direction of its gradient at that point.\n\nSo, we compute $∇f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x+y)+3{z}^{2}x),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x+y)+3{z}^{2}x),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x+y)+3{z}^{2}x)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x+y)+3{z}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x+y),\\,6xz⟩ \\\\ ∇f(1,0,1) & =⟨\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1+0)+3\\cdot {1}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1+0),\\,6\\cdot 1\\cdot 1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+3,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ),\\,6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\pi +3,\\,-1,\\,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function increases most rapidly in the direction of $⟨-\\pi +3,\\,-1,\\,6⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-37080/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff351d3f-449b-5c41-8f72-d1917b2b7536"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37080"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130276/selection/dde26d33537efb94ae644f9a2672c9afe69e4745f4fcb545c4443d462dd77855" :answer/id #uuid "29b174ae-4cbc-5631-8056-f1ecb81bac51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\,i+10\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130276/selection/6da4ff4803b591b19baddb32223008e302d2f91fad112068479f8a0dfde827c2" :answer/id #uuid "e20bb8d1-4a27-53ab-bf11-ee0040b4d41b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i-2\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130276/selection/f75bac4007462c31d674fc5cce95d1bd768df39714ffb52e9b768b79ed61fe38" :answer/id #uuid "8d4ed1dd-5d74-5f08-8bfb-0f4faee446fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,i-5\\,j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130276/selection/6f5de4abdcba53006c0ab69269cb10ed35922e18f567e3b237e9c0ee2f889682" :answer/id #uuid "547282ff-028e-55c8-a319-604d2cad118a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\,i+j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130276/selection/a70a36a19fc6d4f0c69bd789f079a182ed3d121a01bc565cabdd337457c78ade" :answer/id #uuid "e7f19765-8d7a-5f8e-aa4a-c3bfd8539b7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,i+j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130276/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a37980df-1328-5f31-80ff-f01129ef7dbe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130276/selection/dde26d33537efb94ae644f9a2672c9afe69e4745f4fcb545c4443d462dd77855" :answer-field/choices ["q-130276/selection/dde26d33537efb94ae644f9a2672c9afe69e4745f4fcb545c4443d462dd77855" "q-130276/selection/6da4ff4803b591b19baddb32223008e302d2f91fad112068479f8a0dfde827c2" "q-130276/selection/f75bac4007462c31d674fc5cce95d1bd768df39714ffb52e9b768b79ed61fe38" "q-130276/selection/6f5de4abdcba53006c0ab69269cb10ed35922e18f567e3b237e9c0ee2f889682" "q-130276/selection/a70a36a19fc6d4f0c69bd789f079a182ed3d121a01bc565cabdd337457c78ade"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130276" :question/id #uuid "5fca48a5-8fc2-501c-980a-097a661d54fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-130276" :question/problem "In what direction does the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+3xy+2{y}^{2}$ increase most rapidly at the point $(2,1)?$" :question/worked-solution "At a given point, a function $f(x,y)$ increases most rapidly in the direction of its gradient at that point.\n\nSo, we compute $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(2,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+3xy+2{y}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+3xy+2{y}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(2x+3y)\\,i+(3x+4y)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,1) & =(2(2)+3(1))\\,i+(3(2)+4(1))\\,j \\\\  & =7\\,i+10\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function increases most rapidly in the direction of $7\\,i+10\\,j.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130276/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff351d3f-449b-5c41-8f72-d1917b2b7536"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130276"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83554/selection/86917fe2e669f6e856eb9d496eb97bf4e4bff69ca0dcaf93fc9ab79869933b82" :answer/id #uuid "1c992aaf-eb07-5439-8247-2736c78df2f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({e}^{-1}+1)\\text{ }i+({e}^{-1}-1)j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83554/selection/7e5d90cc8d506a22ba190fa1f10bccdd652e87e7288b624f1b13f37cf1e65ac2" :answer/id #uuid "368da0de-e1e4-5a0a-922c-b0744e7b3980" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({e}^{-1}-1)\\text{ }i+{e}^{-1}j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83554/selection/974c817841d5c61967b4b0cd3ebc9dc502949d4d7ac49192c2bd069e1c1d20ea" :answer/id #uuid "315e95ef-eba2-5540-acb6-0190ee0baffa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(e-1)\\text{ }i+ej" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83554/selection/75e1d2985df93b11b9043de7b30194a2e5c4c3feb062ad23c0f5838735fe6ef9" :answer/id #uuid "c247b874-197c-5a17-830b-7cbb40ddf139" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({e}^{-1}+1)\\text{ }i+{e}^{-1}j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83554/selection/0ef35b6e5b9864d2cd72d90c19c8913ed7ae21da0837a2d674505ef028de2a06" :answer/id #uuid "8a140e9d-79e3-5459-9b83-26f805a4c62b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(e+1)\\text{ }i+(e-1)j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83554/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "89ef3c1f-3556-55d4-9634-ffe5bc370834" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83554/selection/7e5d90cc8d506a22ba190fa1f10bccdd652e87e7288b624f1b13f37cf1e65ac2" :answer-field/choices ["q-83554/selection/86917fe2e669f6e856eb9d496eb97bf4e4bff69ca0dcaf93fc9ab79869933b82" "q-83554/selection/7e5d90cc8d506a22ba190fa1f10bccdd652e87e7288b624f1b13f37cf1e65ac2" "q-83554/selection/974c817841d5c61967b4b0cd3ebc9dc502949d4d7ac49192c2bd069e1c1d20ea" "q-83554/selection/75e1d2985df93b11b9043de7b30194a2e5c4c3feb062ad23c0f5838735fe6ef9" "q-83554/selection/0ef35b6e5b9864d2cd72d90c19c8913ed7ae21da0837a2d674505ef028de2a06"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83554" :question/id #uuid "908c4bea-443b-5920-870d-507ba8f31d45" :question/math-academy-id "q-83554" :question/problem "In what direction does the function $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+y{e}^{x}-xy$ increase most rapidly at the point $(-1,1)?$" :question/worked-solution "At a given point, a function $f(x,y)$ increases most rapidly in the direction of its gradient at that point.\n\nSo, we compute $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+y{e}^{x}-xy)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+y{e}^{x}-xy)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y+y{e}^{x}-y)\\text{ }i+(\\frac{x}{y}+{e}^{x}-x)\\text{ }j \\\\ ∇f(1,1) & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+1\\cdot {e}^{-1}-1)\\text{ }i+(\\frac{-1}{1}+{e}^{-1}-(-1))\\text{ }j \\\\  & =({e}^{-1}-1)\\text{ }i+{e}^{-1}j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function increases most rapidly in the direction of $({e}^{-1}-1)\\text{ }i+{e}^{-1}j.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83554/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff351d3f-449b-5c41-8f72-d1917b2b7536"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83554"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186124881 :question/answer-fields 17592186122308] {:db/id "q-36305/selection/ma-v1/b920555e3130745ea949ab7d2f653d55fe502e42b768baa17e777cb2032bb3ec/19a688b075edbd482f1973a02d3d66fa010a85c9243aea5d870e81f32c1101fb" :answer/id #uuid "ee76bc59-b143-5bac-b431-bb48abc4fd61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\pi ,2,\\pi ⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36305/selection/ma-v1/b920555e3130745ea949ab7d2f653d55fe502e42b768baa17e777cb2032bb3ec/fdaf253f7532f4a6f052c3fc859334a5827620893f426c1bf78753a6e1da8387" :answer/id #uuid "42f3c25b-57f9-54fc-89b9-4e1d4ba6655c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\pi ,-1,\\pi ⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36305/selection/ma-v1/b920555e3130745ea949ab7d2f653d55fe502e42b768baa17e777cb2032bb3ec/de97388fc2e6b73254465deb35af33676b6dbab8d6fc894465e8ca05c51cc4d1" :answer/id #uuid "11caf6ea-e88e-501b-8824-ddb49cff3a8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2\\pi ,2,\\pi ⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36305/selection/ma-v1/b920555e3130745ea949ab7d2f653d55fe502e42b768baa17e777cb2032bb3ec/a5973a4351580c125fcd90ef0b148e4720658c91a98fa9a98323d44a2bb6f1b8" :answer/id #uuid "bf3b04a1-94ab-5c54-b6ee-a40a08dc463f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,2,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36305/selection/ma-v1/b920555e3130745ea949ab7d2f653d55fe502e42b768baa17e777cb2032bb3ec/5e35d542c97dd98a5fb83f6400cc5867c6edf1d30400ebda2f98d9422c4a48fc" :answer/id #uuid "4c7976da-3265-5067-a1bb-1e75f8cf9809" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-2\\pi ,-2,-\\pi ⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36305/selection/ma-v1/b920555e3130745ea949ab7d2f653d55fe502e42b768baa17e777cb2032bb3ec" :answer-field/id #uuid "85b43372-9a9f-5d8d-8b56-c1ea0046ec64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36305/selection/ma-v1/b920555e3130745ea949ab7d2f653d55fe502e42b768baa17e777cb2032bb3ec/de97388fc2e6b73254465deb35af33676b6dbab8d6fc894465e8ca05c51cc4d1" :answer-field/choices ["q-36305/selection/ma-v1/b920555e3130745ea949ab7d2f653d55fe502e42b768baa17e777cb2032bb3ec/19a688b075edbd482f1973a02d3d66fa010a85c9243aea5d870e81f32c1101fb" "q-36305/selection/ma-v1/b920555e3130745ea949ab7d2f653d55fe502e42b768baa17e777cb2032bb3ec/fdaf253f7532f4a6f052c3fc859334a5827620893f426c1bf78753a6e1da8387" "q-36305/selection/ma-v1/b920555e3130745ea949ab7d2f653d55fe502e42b768baa17e777cb2032bb3ec/de97388fc2e6b73254465deb35af33676b6dbab8d6fc894465e8ca05c51cc4d1" "q-36305/selection/ma-v1/b920555e3130745ea949ab7d2f653d55fe502e42b768baa17e777cb2032bb3ec/a5973a4351580c125fcd90ef0b148e4720658c91a98fa9a98323d44a2bb6f1b8" "q-36305/selection/ma-v1/b920555e3130745ea949ab7d2f653d55fe502e42b768baa17e777cb2032bb3ec/5e35d542c97dd98a5fb83f6400cc5867c6edf1d30400ebda2f98d9422c4a48fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-36305"] :question/problem "In what direction does the function $g(x,y,z)={y}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x+\\pi z)$ increase most rapidly at the point $(1,1,2)?$" :question/worked-solution "At a given point, a function $g(x,y,z)$ increases most rapidly in the direction of its gradient at that point.\n\nSo, we compute $∇g(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y,z) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x+\\pi z)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x+\\pi z)),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂z}({y}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x+\\pi z))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x+\\pi z),\\,2y,\\,\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x+\\pi z)⟩ \\\\ ∇g(1,1,2) & =⟨2\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi \\cdot 1+\\pi \\cdot 2),\\,2\\cdot 1,\\,\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi \\cdot 1+\\pi \\cdot 2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\pi ),\\,2,\\,\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\pi )⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\pi ,\\,2,\\,\\pi ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function increases most rapidly in the direction of $⟨2\\pi ,\\,2,\\,\\pi ⟩.$" :question/answer-fields ["q-36305/selection/ma-v1/b920555e3130745ea949ab7d2f653d55fe502e42b768baa17e777cb2032bb3ec"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-86537/selection/2f3a2b0e784f45fb99fa9592daa6ddb76021a78eac3484ed1f3b201b658121a8" :answer/id #uuid "c22f01c3-dae7-542c-b484-0de6318f8a3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2i-j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86537/selection/bbd0d8496212cc4d13ce50b6b4a208543163fc14693461fa683ab36ce15d08ef" :answer/id #uuid "0b267b3e-5465-59f4-8c3c-10e417b6cf5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86537/selection/b6144f969338f1e60ba8e079cdbdcfb032baa75af373ede0f30515b185d9fcb2" :answer/id #uuid "017f6928-a034-5b9c-bb5e-035eb7ced53f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86537/selection/0670a6b00db95a7f2759afafc051103c466dd34f434705dd8f5ddd56c342ac9d" :answer/id #uuid "3741d2da-e14f-58c2-8390-902b62b40ea8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i-j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86537/selection/c918677c2f02e59874c54c04e2b4bd6eac89cc7bb5641295b62cabb05e6df3c3" :answer/id #uuid "1446c9fe-1260-5423-8ae4-551a8950f52c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86537/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "186f9b8d-5bd1-5bbc-a54a-0613a65d8d21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86537/selection/bbd0d8496212cc4d13ce50b6b4a208543163fc14693461fa683ab36ce15d08ef" :answer-field/choices ["q-86537/selection/2f3a2b0e784f45fb99fa9592daa6ddb76021a78eac3484ed1f3b201b658121a8" "q-86537/selection/bbd0d8496212cc4d13ce50b6b4a208543163fc14693461fa683ab36ce15d08ef" "q-86537/selection/b6144f969338f1e60ba8e079cdbdcfb032baa75af373ede0f30515b185d9fcb2" "q-86537/selection/0670a6b00db95a7f2759afafc051103c466dd34f434705dd8f5ddd56c342ac9d" "q-86537/selection/c918677c2f02e59874c54c04e2b4bd6eac89cc7bb5641295b62cabb05e6df3c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86537" :question/id #uuid "5e1c6515-4694-552d-8e95-18dee2c7d022" :question/math-academy-id "q-86537" :question/problem "In what direction does the function $f(x,y)=3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ increase most rapidly at the point $(0,1)?$" :question/worked-solution "At a given point, a function $f(x,y)$ increases most rapidly in the direction of its gradient at that point.\n\nSo, we compute $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =(y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\text{ }i+(3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\text{ }j \\\\ ∇f(0,1) & =(1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+6\\cdot 0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))\\text{ }i+(3(0)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))\\text{ }j \\\\  & =-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function increases most rapidly in the direction of $-j.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-86537/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff351d3f-449b-5c41-8f72-d1917b2b7536"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86537"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-37083/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "9f5f7754-33dd-530f-9750-dfe41fde0328" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37083/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "4bf6aae3-1138-5d90-8eb9-c165d7f56024" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37083/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "d86a247c-1534-5a30-876a-7f6322464c9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37083/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "d4323eae-5ac4-58e8-b41d-627a420ef2ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37083/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "9a4ac6bc-381a-509a-b61f-97b7c35e4832" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37083/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1aa780bc-b03f-5573-8318-518efa9363ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-37083/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer-field/choices ["q-37083/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-37083/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-37083/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" "q-37083/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-37083/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-37083" :question/id #uuid "90691e53-4061-50e3-bc0b-ef8fb637c9f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-37083" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=(x+y)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y).$ What is the rate of change of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(2,-1)$ in the direction in which the function decreases most rapidly?" :question/worked-solution "At a given point, a function $f(x,y)$ decreases most rapidly in the opposite direction of its gradient at that point.\n\nIn our case, we compute $-∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(2,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-∇\\,f(x,y) & =-\\frac{∂}{∂x}((x+y)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y))\\text{ }i-\\frac{∂}{∂y}((x+y)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y))\\text{ }j \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)+1)\\text{ }i+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)+1)\\text{ }j \\\\ -∇\\,f(2,-1) & =-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-1)+1)i-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2-1)+1)j \\\\  & =-i-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the rate of change of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(2,-1)$ in the direction of $-∇f(2,-1)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-∇\\,f(2,-1)‖ & =‖-i-j‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-37083/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c330648f-69ad-5778-98cb-bd48a0b160dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37083"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130801/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "a0135bfd-5aa4-5e54-8c91-06a1436467b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130801/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "8df04b1f-42b0-57ad-8752-d0505d9bb43d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130801/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "94303edc-c45c-5675-a475-72c88e4fbfc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130801/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "88dc4d39-4bfc-56d4-90e6-65415aa09257" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130801/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "c797a65e-afbd-5b9c-af24-7c12ee36fbd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130801/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c7afa458-96db-5d55-9c98-3c6f654f4d5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130801/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-130801/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-130801/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-130801/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" "q-130801/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-130801/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130801" :question/id #uuid "62433894-eb6d-5153-9489-351a9fe549d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-130801" :question/problem "Consider the function $g(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{y}{x}.$ What is the rate of change of $g(x,y)$ at the point $(-1,1)$ in the direction of the vector $v=⟨1,-\\sqrt{2}⟩?$" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of $g(x,y)$ at the point $(-1,1)$ in the direction of $v$ is equal to the directional derivative ${g}_{u}^{′}(-1,1).$ \n\nFirst, we find the unit vector $u$ in the direction of $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-\\sqrt{2})^{2}}=\\sqrt{3} \\\\ u & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨1,-\\sqrt{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient $∇g(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{y}{x}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x}{y}+\\frac{y}{x})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{y}-\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}⟩ \\\\ ∇g(-1,1) & =⟨\\frac{1}{1}-\\frac{1}{(-1)^{2}},\\frac{1}{(-1)}-\\frac{(-1)}{{1}^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the directional derivative ${g}_{u}^{′}(-1,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{u}^{′}(-1,1) & =∇g(-1,1)\\cdot u \\\\  & =⟨0,0⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨1,-\\sqrt{2}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{0(1)+0(-\\sqrt{2})}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130801/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c330648f-69ad-5778-98cb-bd48a0b160dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130801"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83613/selection/f2df4777bc72011379546daa70a30d3acde31d976763c26d3f5382a15b9d7099" :answer/id #uuid "3023fb85-7f8e-557f-8b4a-2923ca99c63f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(\\pi -2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83613/selection/cd05cf5a26f880a3d9ded5e2e980f06d8cff5d6142622be4022bfc549f0f63ac" :answer/id #uuid "c5044a50-4447-5400-b459-f9317a49bc64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}(\\pi +2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83613/selection/c5967b8e0d7ba8b0a86cbce459341e7158eb8d0bad9cccb0bed6562ffa0d92cd" :answer/id #uuid "db68217b-436e-5bec-9776-965472658894" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}(\\pi -2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83613/selection/b86ddc8b2915c311f8cde74e100ed3a5dff5870378af83fdc492a4c408174711" :answer/id #uuid "9c2169d0-f362-5b0f-8c3d-26181fbd68c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(\\pi +2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83613/selection/ec029fc82ee0db4f12e33df49d707abb81fb01a33e2c08f0c2d38bcc719643df" :answer/id #uuid "eb266df5-9daf-5687-906c-193075a88abe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi -\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83613/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f825ffc-8232-57b0-90f2-fed9245285e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83613/selection/c5967b8e0d7ba8b0a86cbce459341e7158eb8d0bad9cccb0bed6562ffa0d92cd" :answer-field/choices ["q-83613/selection/f2df4777bc72011379546daa70a30d3acde31d976763c26d3f5382a15b9d7099" "q-83613/selection/cd05cf5a26f880a3d9ded5e2e980f06d8cff5d6142622be4022bfc549f0f63ac" "q-83613/selection/c5967b8e0d7ba8b0a86cbce459341e7158eb8d0bad9cccb0bed6562ffa0d92cd" "q-83613/selection/b86ddc8b2915c311f8cde74e100ed3a5dff5870378af83fdc492a4c408174711" "q-83613/selection/ec029fc82ee0db4f12e33df49d707abb81fb01a33e2c08f0c2d38bcc719643df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83613" :question/id #uuid "87567443-ec6a-5071-9f0c-ac11c5afa2b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-83613" :question/problem "Consider the function $g(x,y)=2x\\operatorname{tan}⁡y-2y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$ What is the rate of change of $g(x,y)$ at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ in the direction of the vector $v=⟨-1,1⟩?$" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of $g(x,y)$ at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ in the direction of $v$ is equal to the directional derivative ${g}_{u}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ \n\nFirst, we find the unit vector $u$ in the direction of $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ u & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient $∇\\,g(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,g(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x\\operatorname{tan}⁡y-2y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\operatorname{tan}⁡y-2y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{tan}⁡y-2y{sec}^{2}⁡x,\\,2x{sec}^{2}⁡y-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x⟩ \\\\ ∇\\,g(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =⟨2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot {sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}\\cdot {sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\cdot 1-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 2,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2-\\pi ,\\,\\pi -2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the directional derivative ${g}_{u}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{u}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =∇\\,g(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\cdot u \\\\  & =⟨2-\\pi ,\\pi -2⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{(2-\\pi )\\cdot (-1)+(\\pi -2)\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi -4}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}(\\pi -2).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-83613/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c330648f-69ad-5778-98cb-bd48a0b160dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83613"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83608/selection/c71471265c459db429c0904073d51b98263c5556bf8642fd8ee00873955333bc" :answer/id #uuid "d74e46a2-b98e-5792-a519-12a731e04560" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi \\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83608/selection/63079cc748dc757e7a8e5256fd2c9d955e6cf36193b2548b0f6e7b6b72fbf55c" :answer/id #uuid "b300e76e-dac5-5178-8d06-57c2b767e0a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83608/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "6def077c-81d2-5fff-bdc9-37b29fbcf404" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83608/selection/0c3d46cceb3dc5e2e3f4eba7c642c51c944695c1ebca2bd4c3b41ea3717a3e68" :answer/id #uuid "0291e86d-e6ef-51c5-8cd8-beaa672aa63e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83608/selection/e65264720c59aa6cf4dec4ef6ab354eac2177abff5c6282da5c317519a0708d0" :answer/id #uuid "dc6dbd1c-86e4-529c-8380-ae91f6ffbe45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83608/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b270d00-5f3c-5636-9b99-f29ddea55a3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-83608/selection/e65264720c59aa6cf4dec4ef6ab354eac2177abff5c6282da5c317519a0708d0" :answer-field/choices ["q-83608/selection/c71471265c459db429c0904073d51b98263c5556bf8642fd8ee00873955333bc" "q-83608/selection/63079cc748dc757e7a8e5256fd2c9d955e6cf36193b2548b0f6e7b6b72fbf55c" "q-83608/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" "q-83608/selection/0c3d46cceb3dc5e2e3f4eba7c642c51c944695c1ebca2bd4c3b41ea3717a3e68" "q-83608/selection/e65264720c59aa6cf4dec4ef6ab354eac2177abff5c6282da5c317519a0708d0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-83608" :question/id #uuid "26233936-7690-5f63-84cf-a5a4e6f7c30f" :question/math-academy-id "q-83608" :question/problem "Consider the function $g(x,y)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)}{y}+\\pi xy.$ What is the rate of change of $g(x,y)$ at the point $(1,1)$ in the direction of the vector $v=⟨-2,2⟩?$" :question/worked-solution "The rate of change of $g(x,y)$ at the point $(1,1)$ in the direction of $v$ is equal to the directional derivative ${g}_{u}^{′}(1,1).$ \n\nFirst, we find the unit vector $u$ in the direction of $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}=2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ u & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient $∇\\,g(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,g(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)}{y}+\\pi xy),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)}{y}+\\pi xy)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)}{y}+\\pi y,\\,-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)}{{y}^{2}}+\\pi x⟩ \\\\ ∇\\,g(1,1) & =⟨\\frac{\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1)}{1}+\\pi \\cdot 1,\\,-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi \\cdot 1)}{{1}^{2}}+\\pi \\cdot 1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\pi +\\pi ,0+\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\pi ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the directional derivative ${g}_{u}^{′}(1,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{u}^{′}(1,1) & =∇\\,g(1,1)\\cdot u \\\\  & =⟨0,\\pi ⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot (-1)+\\pi \\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-83608/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c330648f-69ad-5778-98cb-bd48a0b160dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83608"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-36300/selection/ed480161c278cf263b7506697b7b27c19b2594926ada6527945331e6eb5a4b3b" :answer/id #uuid "da493b2b-9d48-57e0-82ee-bdf854cc43cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36300/selection/a246711f2d8b2088a365ebe7aa3f1c85e460b4e74af35406d4bd79ef45396e9a" :answer/id #uuid "269b3df3-6718-5e56-95a7-04bec75742f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{82}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36300/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "fd4a9e24-005a-5dfb-8480-4713eb0fefba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36300/selection/4ef0fcc340e40ad6bcef1c832215cd28abf240aabeed43296dfece28d20d1935" :answer/id #uuid "535f9046-a320-57a6-a8a3-35c141a42407" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36300/selection/f97ca8e06f2e6d5cce38559e6b5e49f6e0c27eacd8125be588adfebd409ef921" :answer/id #uuid "b6290e81-7555-5c3a-a4d9-f162c0d81c96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{80}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36300/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f126513-a801-56d0-a2c4-55b140281628" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36300/selection/a246711f2d8b2088a365ebe7aa3f1c85e460b4e74af35406d4bd79ef45396e9a" :answer-field/choices ["q-36300/selection/ed480161c278cf263b7506697b7b27c19b2594926ada6527945331e6eb5a4b3b" "q-36300/selection/a246711f2d8b2088a365ebe7aa3f1c85e460b4e74af35406d4bd79ef45396e9a" "q-36300/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-36300/selection/4ef0fcc340e40ad6bcef1c832215cd28abf240aabeed43296dfece28d20d1935" "q-36300/selection/f97ca8e06f2e6d5cce38559e6b5e49f6e0c27eacd8125be588adfebd409ef921"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-36300" :question/id #uuid "0d871812-574c-5223-8f52-1d1e692d14a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-36300" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=2xy+{e}^{3x-y}.$ What is the rate of change of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,3)$ in the direction in which the function decreases most rapidly?" :question/worked-solution "At a given point, a function $f(x,y)$ decreases most rapidly in the opposite direction of its gradient at that point.\n\nIn our case, we compute $-∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-∇\\,f(x,y) & =-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2xy+{e}^{3x-y})\\text{ }i-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy+{e}^{3x-y})\\text{ }j \\\\  & =-(2y+3{e}^{3x-y})\\text{ }i-(2x-{e}^{3x-y})\\text{ }j \\\\ -∇\\,f(1,3) & =-(2\\cdot 3+3\\cdot {e}^{3\\cdot 1-3})\\text{ }i-(2\\cdot 1-{e}^{3\\cdot 1-3})\\text{ }j \\\\  & =-9\\text{ }i-\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the rate of change of $f(x,y)$ at the point $(1,3)$ in the direction of $-∇f(1,3)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-∇\\,f(1,3)‖ & =‖-9\\text{ }i-\\text{ }j‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-9)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{82}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-36300/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c330648f-69ad-5778-98cb-bd48a0b160dd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-36300"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3377"] :question/problem "Find the directional derivative of the function $g(x, y) =3x^2+4xy$ at the point $A(0,1)$ in the direction towards the point $B(1,4).$" :question/worked-solution "The directional derivative $g'_{\\mathbf u}(a,b)$ of a function $g(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $\\mathbf v$ is given by\n\n$$\ng'_{\\mathbf u}(a,b) = \\nabla g(a,b)\\cdot\\mathbf u\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $\\mathbf v.$\n\nFirst, we find the direction vector and the corresponding unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,4⟩-⟨0,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,3⟩ \\\\ u & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}}{‖\\overset{\\to }{AB}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}}}⟨1,3⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the gradient $\\nabla g(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $A(0,1)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}+4xy),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}+4xy)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6x+4y,\\,4x⟩ \\\\ ∇g(0,1) & =⟨6\\cdot 0+4\\cdot 1,\\,4\\cdot 0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{u}^{′}(0,1) & =∇g(0,1)\\cdot u \\\\  & =⟨4,0⟩\\cdot ⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}},\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{10}}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{10}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3381"] :question/problem "In what direction does the function $f (x, y) = \\ln (x^2y)$ decrease most rapidly at the point $(2, 1)?$" :question/worked-solution "At a given point, a function $f(x,y)$ decreases most rapidly in the direction opposite to that of its gradient.\n\nSo, we compute $-\\nabla f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(2,1)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-∇f(x,y) & =-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}y))\\text{ }i-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}y))\\text{ }j \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}y}\\cdot 2xy\\text{ }i-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}y}\\cdot {x}^{2}j \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{x}\\text{ }i-\\frac{1}{y}\\text{ }j \\\\ -∇f(2,1) & =-\\frac{2}{2}\\text{ }i-\\frac{1}{1}\\text{ }j \\\\  & =-i-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function decreases most rapidly in the direction of $- \\, \\mathbf i - \\mathbf j.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3382"] :question/problem "Consider the function $g (x, y) = \\ln \\left(\\sqrt {xy^3}\\right).$ What is the rate of change of $g$ at the point $\\left(\\dfrac 12, \\dfrac 32 \\right)$ in the direction in which the function increases most rapidly?" :question/worked-solution "At a given point, a function $g(x,y)$ increases most rapidly in the direction of its gradient at that point.\n\nIn our case, we compute $\\nabla g(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $\\left(\\dfrac 12, \\dfrac 32 \\right)\\!\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{x{y}^{3}})),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{x{y}^{3}}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x{y}^{3}}}\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{3}}{2\\sqrt{x{y}^{3}}},\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x{y}^{3}}}\\cdot \\frac{3x{y}^{2}}{2\\sqrt{x{y}^{3}}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2x},\\,\\frac{3}{2y}⟩ \\\\ ∇g(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2}) & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2})},\\frac{3}{2\\cdot (\\frac{3}{2})}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the rate of change of $g(x,y)$ at the point $\\left(\\dfrac 12, \\dfrac 32 \\right)$ in the direction of $\\nabla g\\left(\\dfrac 12, \\dfrac 32 \\right)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖∇g(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2})‖ & =‖⟨1,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
